ormat="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>5039345</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-8092341-A"  status="new"><document-id status="new"  format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>8092341</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A"  name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </patcit><patcit ucid="US-5624979-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>US</country><doc-number>5624979</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id> <sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </patcit> </patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1167417A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKUMURA HIROYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKEDA CHEMICAL INDUSTRIES LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKEUCHI HIROSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UCHIDA TOSHIAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKUMURA, HIROYA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKEDA CHEMICAL INDUSTRIES, LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKEUCHI, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UCHIDA, TOSHIAKI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKUMURA HIROYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKEUCHI HIROSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UCHIDA TOSHIAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKUMURA, HIROYA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKEUCHI, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UCHIDA, TOSHIAKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Flame-retardant vinyl esters which are prepared either by reacting an epoxy compound (A) with a cyclic phosphorus compound such as 9,10-dihydro-9-oxa-10-phosphaphenanthrene-10-oxide at a P-H/epoxy ratio of 0.01 to 0.7 and then reacting the remaining epoxy groups with an ethylenically unsaturated monobasic acid (B) or by reacting the compound (A) with the acid (B) and then reacting the resulting product with the phosphorus compound at a P-H/epoxy ratio of 0.01 to 0.7, and have phosphorus contents ranging from 0.1 to 6 wt. % and double bond equivalents ranging from 200 to 1000 g/mol. The esters can give cured products which have high flame retardance, heat resistance, and humidity resistance and excellent mechanical properties and are useful for laminated sheets and resist inks, in spite of their being free from halogen.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne des vinylesters retardateurs de flamme que l'on prépare soit en faisant réagir un composé époxy (A) avec un composé phosphoré cyclique tel que 9,10-dihydro-9-oxa-10-phosphaphénanthrène-10-oxyde selon un rapport P-H/époxy compris entre 0,01 et 0,7, puis en faisant réagir les groupes époxy restants avec un acide monobasique (B) éthyléniquement insaturé, ou en faisant réagir le composé (A) avec l'acide (B), puis en faisant réagir le produit obtenu avec le composé phosphoré selon un rapport P-H/époxy compris entre 0,01 et 0,7. Lesdits vinylesters se caractérisent par une teneur en phosphore comprise entre 0,1 et 6 % en poids, et par des équivalents doubles liaisons compris entre 200 et 1000g/mol. Ces esters permettent d'obtenir des produits durcis caractérisés par une grande ininflammabilité, une bonne résistance à la chaleur et à l'humidité, et d'excellentes propriétés mécaniques. Quoiqu'exempts d'halogène, ces esters sont utilisés dans les stratifiés en planche et les encres à résist.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>